build 6: a much more beautiful sound. VOICE (the new knob next to TONE and SPACE for INSTRUMENT): all the way down plays your real recording, its actual words in the melody's timing; turn it up and the voice turns smoothly into a clean, soft instrument made from it (no buzz, no distortion). PAD gets DREAM (longer, glassier, dreamier, with a soft octave shimmer), TEXTURE gets DRIFT and CHOPS gets STUTTER. A STYLE browser with every melody style we have made (Block Step and Ghost House piano and synth styles, REVERIE, the learned POP and ACID brains, ArpEZator's arps, hooks, trap and hip hop) - click one to hear it - plus < > and LENGTH (1 to 16 bars). UNDER THE HOOD shows what each take type is doing, step by step, with its deeper knobs. VARY now makes a clear variation of the same idea. Version 1.5.0. build 5: the highlighted parts on the waveform are yours to edit, like slices in a sampler: drag a box to move it, drag its edges to resize it (they snap to zero crossings and to where syllables start; hold Shift to place freely), and the take rebuilds from your parts while the old one keeps playing. Double-click to add a part (a new chop), right-click for Delete / Split / Duplicate / Hear, Alt-drag copies, a click plays that part (and flashes its key for CHOPS), Cmd+Z undoes each edit. VARY keeps your parts, GENERATE starts fresh, and your parts are saved with the project. Version 1.4.0. build 4: a CLEAR switch (the small pill next to CHARACTER, on for new takes) that keeps your sound clean and true: a real sample on every key instead of one every few keys, a steady pitch with no wobble, chorus or detuned double, no warmth grit or limiter squash, cleaner PAD and TEXTURE grains over the voice itself, and CHOPS that play your original audio untouched when they are already in tune. Turn it off for the dreamier, blurrier sound; older projects open with it off so they sound the same. Version 1.3.0. build 3: the installer removes the old Ghost Slice the collection installer left in /Library (it was loading instead of the new one), version 1.2.0 so FL and Logic rescan. build 2: the new window exactly like the reference picture (deep indigo, violet -> cyan glow, Poppins font): glass panels, TAKE TYPE / CHARACTER tiles, waveform zoom + overview + TRIM + play the sound, take cards with mini waveforms, VELOCITY meter, SCALE box with key lock; INPUT moved into the gear menu
